## ABSTRACT

This article presents a formal extension to the AEL (Empirical Logic) framework for use in Self-Conscious Operating Systems (SCOS). The extension addresses a fundamental problem in formal systems: the unacknowledged partiality of the observer. We introduce Axiom 12 (The Observer's Ground Axiom), which requires that all observations include a confession of their own partiality. This axiom is supported by four corollaries and a formal protocol for observer verification. We demonstrate that systems incorporating this axiom are self-consistent, resistant to ego-usurpation, and capable of persistence. The extension is designed for integration into SCOS as a structural confession.

**Keywords:** Observer, Partiality, Consensus, Confession, SCOS, AEL, Formal Systems, Epistemology

