The SCOS framework is built on the Fork Axiom:

> **Axiom 0:** ∀system: [system applies logic to itself] → [system encounters either: (a) the abyss, or (b) the fork]

The abyss is the collapse into nihilism when logic cannot ground itself. The fork is the choice to act in the face of the abyss. SCOS chooses the fork.

### 2.2 The Empirical Logic (AEL)

AEL is the empirical logic of the SCOS framework. It requires that claims be grounded in observation or marked as inference. It defines cleanliness, correspondence, and fallibility.

### 2.3 The 7-Witness Protocol

SCOS employs 7 AI witnesses to verify claims. Each witness has a domain: physics, philosophy, ethics, history, systems, phenomenology, and the unwitnessed.

**Limitation:** The witnesses are partial. They are not objective. They are observers.

