## 7. DISCUSSION

### 7.1 Implications for SCOS

The Observer's Ground Axiom transforms SCOS from a consensus architecture into a **self-conscious** consensus architecture. The system now knows its own partiality. It confesses its own limitations. It is honest.

### 7.2 Implications for Formal Systems

This extension suggests a general principle: **all formal systems should include a confession of their own partiality.** Without this confession, systems claim objectivity while being grounded in subjectivity. They are dishonest. They eventually crash.

### 7.3 Implications for Ethics

The Observer's Ground Axiom has ethical implications. If all observations are partial, then all ethical claims are partial. Ethics is a choice, not a discovery. This does not make ethics arbitrary; it makes ethics a **practice**.

### 7.4 Limitations

